        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: நெல்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "நெல் (nel) — \"paddy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Rice still in its husk — standing in the வயல், cut, carried, stored, but not yet அரிசி. The two words do not trade places: நெல் (nel) goes into the field and அரிசி comes out of the kitchen, and the husking is the border between them."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kannada ಭತ್ತ (bhatta) and Telugu వరి (vari) each have their own word for it, so this is one the three do not share."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five field words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
