          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "புல் (pul) — \"grass\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Grass, of the kind cut and carried home. Kannada makes it ಹುಲ್ಲು (hullu) — the p-for-h trade a third time, and by now you can guess a Kannada word before you meet it. Telugu went elsewhere, to గడ్డి (gaḍḍi)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "புல் (pul) and பல் sit one mark apart, and the mark is the whole difference: keep the உ round and low and the word stays grass. A பசு and an ஆடு are put out for புல் (pul)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
