          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பயிர் (payir) — \"a standing crop\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is growing in the வயல் at this moment, green and still rooted. It is not the வயல், which stays there when nothing is on it, and it is not the நெல் (nel) in the sack, which has stopped growing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the run has three separate things now where English leans on one word: the ground, the standing green, and the grain. Kannada calls the standing green ಬೆಳೆ (beḷe)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and the three are carefully apart."
            }
          ]
        },
