              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "களம் (kaḷam) — \"a threshing floor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The beaten flat ground at the edge of a village where cut நெல் (nel) is spread, trodden and winnowed. Telugu has the same word as కల్లం (kallaṁ), which makes it old."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is not காலம், the season word you already have. This one is short at the front and takes the ள; காலம் opens long and takes the ல. One mark and one letter, and they are unrelated."
            }
          ]
        },
