              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அறுவடை (aṟuvaṭai) — \"the harvest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The cutting and the gathering together, and the stretch of the year named after them. Kannada ಸುಗ್ಗಿ (suggi) and Telugu పంట (paṇṭa) each named the same weeks their own way."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The front of it is the reaping, not the ஆறு you counted with: this one opens short on அ and takes the hard ற straight away, where six opens long on ஆ. Close together on the page, far apart in the mouth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run is closed: paddy, grass, a standing crop, a threshing floor, and the harvest."
            }
          ]
        },
